1	//! Interface chains and named types resolved once per run and shared by every component that reaches them.
2	//!
3	//! A non-generic interface's chain depends on more than the interface: on the component's cycle sets (an ancestor
4	//! already being resolved cuts a branch short), on the type parameters in scope, on the component's own parameter
5	//! defaults, and on the depth it is reached at. So a recording keeps every read the resolution made of those
6	//! (`StateReads`), and another component reuses it only when its own state gives the same answer to each one. Then
7	//! the resolution would take exactly the same steps, so the recording replays its effects instead: the chain itself,
8	//! with its props shared rather than copied, its diagnostics, the cycle-set additions, whether it showed
9	//! an unevaluated alias by name, and the files watch mode must re-resolve the component for.
10	//!
11	//! Only the first read of a key says what the state held on entry: a later one may see what the resolution itself
12	//! added, which a replay adds again.
13	//!
14	//! A recording keeps each distinct diagnostic once. Resolution reports one each time it meets the cause, the output
15	//! merges identical diagnostics, and nothing in resolution reads them back, so only the first of each matters; keeping
16	//! every copy, again in each recording that encloses it, took gigabytes on Chakra with dependencies loaded.
17	
18	use std::hash::Hash;
19	use std::sync::{Arc, Condvar, Mutex, PoisonError};
20	use std::thread::ThreadId;
21	use std::time::Duration;
22	
23	use compact_str::CompactString;
24	use rustc_hash::FxHashSet;
25	
26	use crate::types::{ComponentMapping, Diagnostic, ResolveState, StateReads};
27	
